# Human-edited dependency input (runbook §5.3).
# Regenerate the hash-locked output with:  bin/lock-dev-deps.sh --update
# Verify it is current with:               bin/lock-dev-deps.sh --check
#
# Note (plan §5, documented assumption): httpx and pydantic are required by
# runbook §8.1's minimum list but are not imported anywhere in Session 1.
# They are locked here for spec compliance; the cost is a wider hash-lock
# surface than Session 1 alone needs.

pytest
pytest-timeout
pytest-xdist
PyYAML
jsonschema
httpx

# Pinned, and it is the only tool here that is (Session 6, Run 7).
#
# `--check` re-resolves this file and compares, so an unpinned entry means the
# gate goes red the next time upstream publishes -- through nobody's change. It
# has happened twice, both times with ruff, both times because a new release
# formatted something differently from the one the tree was formatted with.
# Pinning the formatter makes "the tree is formatted" a statement about a
# specific formatter rather than about whichever one resolved today.
#
# The others are left floating deliberately rather than by omission: none has
# ever produced a red gate, and pinning a test runner is a maintenance
# commitment that belongs with the CI job ADR 0019 specifies and nobody has
# built (§10). Recorded as a decision so the next reader does not read the
# inconsistency as an oversight.
ruff==0.16.3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session 6, Run 7. The auth service's runtime set, in the development
# environment because its unit tests need the real libraries.
#
# SEC-CRED-002 is a `contract`-mode requirement that reads the Argon2id profile
# back FROM THE ENCODED HASH. There is no way to satisfy that without producing
# an encoded hash, which means argon2-cffi has to be installed here and not
# only in the image. The same is true of every measured claim in Run 7's
# batteries: PyJWT's unbounded header parse, psycopg-pool's `open=False`,
# pydantic's `extra="forbid"`. A test that mocked them would be a test about
# the mock (ADR 0065, arriving for the fifth time).
#
# EVERY VERSION HERE IS PINNED TO versions.in.yaml, and
# `test_the_development_environment_installs_the_locked_service_versions`
# asserts the two agree. Two files naming one version is this repository's
# recurring defect; a test computing the relation is the only thing that has
# ever stopped it. Unpinned entries would let uv resolve something newer than
# the image runs, and the offline suite would then be measuring a version this
# product does not ship.
#
# psycopg[binary] rather than a bare psycopg: measured in Run 7, the bare
# distribution installs and then raises `ImportError: no pq wrapper available`
# because there is no libpq on the machine (ADR 0083).
argon2-cffi==25.1.0
cryptography==50.0.0
fastapi==0.121.2
psycopg[binary]==3.3.4
psycopg-pool==3.3.1
pydantic==2.13.4
pydantic-settings==2.14.2
pyjwt==2.13.0
uvicorn==0.50.2
